            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent recipe....only change I made was to use mascarpone cheese and double the strawberries :). I put the glaze in a Baggie, cut the tip off and squeezed on to top of pie, much easier that way!",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-12T09:02:02.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ReneePaj"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is very easy and delicious. I made my own graham cracker crust. Used powdered sugar in the cream cheese mixture in place of the granulated sugar and added about a cup of cool whip free for texture. This turns out to be a relatively lower calorie and lower fat dessert with lots of goodness from fresh strawberries. A definite keeper! I will be making this again!",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-01T15:40:56.183Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "EmiEmi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed one reviewer's recommendation to use Mascarpone cheese instead, and highly recommend! I have made this pie three times in five days for different audiences (tested the pie on my husband, co-workers, and one friend who wants dessert ideas for a summertime bridal shower) and all have given it rave reviews! It's delicious and light - a perfect summertime dessert staple!",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-06T13:50:18.060Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Becky"
            },
            "reviewBody": "You had me at \"Strawberry, and pie\". YUM. The ONLY thing I do differently is use less of the glaze. I only use enough to lightly coat the berries on top to kind of \"gel\" things together. This is so refreshing, not overly sweet, and perfect for any summer get-together. If you like strawberries, graham cracker crust, and rich, creamy cheeses...........then this is for you. :) (P.S.- I know in some areas Neufchatel would be difficult to find. You can use any smooth &amp; creamy cheese. Just add less or more depending on the richness &amp; consistency).",
            "datePublished": "2013-05-30T17:15:58.317Z"
